## Error Handling Architecture

### 1. Centralized Error Handling
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE error handling
// Centralized error handling with helper functions
try {
  const result = await executeQuery(query, params);
  sendSuccessResponse(res, result.rows[0], 'OPERATION_TYPE', duration);
} catch (error) {
  sendErrorResponse(res, error, 'Operation failed');
}

// ❌ MANUAL error handling
// Inconsistent error handling across routes
try {
  const result = await executeQuery(query, params);
  res.status(200).json({ success: true, data: result.rows[0] });
} catch (error) {
  logger.error('Error:', error);
  res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: 'Operation failed' });
}
```

### 2. Frontend Error Boundaries
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE error boundaries
// Simple error boundary with fallback UI
class ErrorBoundary extends React.Component {
  constructor(props) {
    super(props);
    this.state = { hasError: false };
  }
  
  static getDerivedStateFromError(error) {
    return { hasError: true };
  }
  
  render() {
    if (this.state.hasError) {
      return <div>Something went wrong.</div>;
    }
    
    return this.props.children;
  }
}

// ❌ OVER-ENGINEERED error handling
// Complex error tracking system
const errorTracker = new ErrorTracker({
  providers: [
    new SentryProvider({ dsn: process.env.SENTRY_DSN }),
    new BugsnagProvider({ apiKey: process.env.BUGSNAG_API_KEY })
  ],
  filters: [
    new ErrorFilter({ minLevel: 'error' }),
    new RateLimitFilter({ maxPerMinute: 100 })
  ]
});
```

