## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Over-Engineering
- Complex state management for simple data
- Microservices for monolithic application
- Advanced caching for small datasets
- Complex authentication for simple use case
- Over-optimization of simple queries

### ❌ Under-Engineering
- No error handling
- No input validation
- No performance monitoring
- No testing
- No security considerations

## Scale-Appropriate Patterns

### ✅ Right-Sized Solutions
- React Query for API state management
- Simple in-memory caching with TTL
- Cookie-based authentication
- Raw SQL with connection pooling
- Basic error handling and logging
- Focused component architecture
- Appropriate test coverage
- WebSocket for real-time updates
- PWA capabilities for mobile experience

## Remember: Choose architecture patterns that match the actual scale and requirements, not theoretical maximums or over-engineering patterns.